<section class="atl-about">
  <h2 class="ref-sec-title">About the timeline</h2>
  <p>The timeline draws the <a href="/state/">states register</a>: every state, empire, principality and chiefdom the Institute has recorded, with the years it existed, grouped by region. Bars in the same row never overlap, so each row reads as a line of succession only by chance; follow the <a href="/connections">connections</a> for who succeeded whom. Years before the common era are often approximate, and many early states are known only from a few sources.</p>
  <p>For the world in a single year, open the <a href="/atlas">atlas</a> or a <a href="/years/">year page</a>; for an age, the <a href="/centuries/">century pages</a>; for the people of each age, <a href="/people/">People in History</a>.</p>
</section>
